# Section 15.4 exit($code: Int): Never -- terminates the program with the given
# code, flushing stdout first (like panic). The "before exit" line is flushed
# and appears; the line after exit is unreachable and never prints. The chosen
# code (5) becomes the process exit status, so both engines must agree on stdout
# AND exit code. exit is Never-typed, so it satisfies main's Unit return without
# producing a value.
sub main(): Unit {
    print("before exit")
    exit(5)
    print("unreachable after exit")
}
